---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = 'July 19, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BBCamMaster Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the BBCamMaster browser extension. BBCamMaster collects no data, has no servers, and makes no third-party network requests."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/bbcammaster">BBCamMaster</a></p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="policy">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="card summary">
        <p>
          <strong>BBCamMaster does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data.</strong>
          It has no servers, no analytics, no tracking, and makes no network requests to
          any third party.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What the extension accesses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>paramountplus.com pages only.</strong> BBCamMaster runs solely on
          paramountplus.com, as declared in its manifest. It does not run on any other
          website.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The page’s video player.</strong> To provide its features — cam switching,
          focus cam, audio isolation, theater mode, quality control, and keyboard shortcuts —
          the extension reads and modifies the content of the Paramount+ live feed pages and
          interacts with the page’s existing video player. This happens entirely within your
          browser.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        BBCamMaster saves two small, non-personal values in your browser’s local storage so
        the extension works smoothly:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The URLs of the Big Brother camera channels it discovers on the page.</li>
        <li>Your preferred focus-cam window size and position.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information never leaves your device and is not associated with you. You can
        clear it at any time by removing the extension or clearing site data for
        paramountplus.com.
      </p>

      <h2>Data the extension does not collect</h2>
      <p>
        BBCamMaster does not collect or transmit: personally identifiable information,
        authentication credentials, financial information, health information, location,
        browsing history, communications, or usage and behavioral analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        BBCamMaster does not sell, share, or transfer any user data to third parties,
        because it does not collect any user data.
      </p>

      <h2>Paramount+ / CBS</h2>
      <p>
        BBCamMaster is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Paramount, CBS,
        Viacom, or the Big Brother production. It requires your own active Paramount+
        subscription and does not access, decrypt, record, or redistribute video streams.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Any future change to this policy will be reflected on this page with an updated date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be directed to the developer via
        <a href="/contact">dane.codes/contact</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 100px 0 40px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-bg) 0%, var(--color-surface) 100%);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .page-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .container.narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .policy {
    padding: 32px 0 48px;
  }

  .summary {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
  }

  .policy p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .policy ul {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
